{"t": 1795083267.9297965, "tool": "analyze", "code": "from scipy.optimize import least_squares\ny=dA_dt\ndef f1(p): return p[0]*A**p[1]/(p[2]+A**p[1]) + p[3]*t**p[4]*A**p[5] + p[6]*t**p[7]*A**p[8]\ndef f2(p): return p[0]*A**p[1]/(p[2]+A**p[1]) + p[3]*t**p[4]*A**p[5] + p[6]*t**p[7]*np.exp(-p[8]*A)\ndef f3(p): return p[0]*A**p[1]/(p[2]+A**p[1]) + p[3]*t**p[4]*A**p[5] + p[6]*np.exp(p[7]*t)*np.exp(-p[8]*A)\nrng=np.random.default_rng(0)\nfor f,name in [(f1,'pow'),(f2,'exp'),(f3,'expexp')]:\n    best=None\n    for i in range(25):\n        p0=rng.uniform(0.2,2,9)*np.array([5,1,2,-.1,1,.3,.01,2,2] if i%2 else [1]*9)\n        if i%2==0: p0[3]*=-1\n        try:\n            r=least_squares(lambda p:f(p)-y,p0,max_nfev=3000)\n        except Exception as e: continue\n        if best is None or r.cost<best.cost: best=r\n    print(name,2*best.cost/len(y)/y.var(),best.x.round(4))\n", "out": "pow 4.997880676170539e-24 [ 6.5563e+00  2.0000e+00  3.3113e+00 -9.3500e-02  2.0000e+00  0.0000e+00\n  4.5000e-03  3.0000e+00 -1.0000e+00]\nexp 0.00206892128580025 [ 7.1361  1.9452  3.7792 -0.1035  1.7462  0.2836  0.0095  3.6339  4.5077]\nexpexp 0.0027820037690606033 [ 7.1253  1.9757  3.8696 -0.1023  1.7441  0.2993  0.3427  0.5017  4.8078]\n"}
